    "procedure": "Count equal forward pairs at lags one through five, then independently shuffle each page's fixed rune multiset 2,000 times.",
    "parameters": "No page crossing or circular wrap; 2,000 seeded shuffles; exact expected counts and nearest-rank central intervals.",
    "exclusions": "Alternative transcriptions, word-internal only pairs, other lags, cipher-key simulations, plaintext inference, corrected multiple-testing claims."
  },
  "outcome": "supported",
  "finding": "The observed adjacency deficit is not a comparable deficit at rune lags two through five under this specified page-shuffle reference.",
  "limitations": "Exploratory: lag-one suppression was already known. Fixed-count page shuffles are not a model of English or a specific cipher. The source is an archived transcription; human review pending.",
  "next_steps": "Check boundary-sensitive versions and competing cipher models as separately frozen variants; audit uncertain source glyphs before making stronger claims.",
